Subtask 3.3: Create Custom Health Monitoring
Let's create a more sophisticated monitoring setup.

Create a health check service
Create a file called health-monitor-service.yaml:

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: vm-health-monitor
  namespace: vm-health-probes
spec:
  selector:
    app: webserver-full-probes
  ports:
  - name: http
    port: 80
    targetPort: 80
  type: ClusterIP
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: health-check-script
  namespace: vm-health-probes
data:
  check-health.sh: |
    #!/bin/bash
    VM_SERVICE="vm-health-monitor"
    NAMESPACE="vm-health-probes"
    
    while true; do
        echo "$(date): Checking VM health..."
        
        if curl -s -f http://$VM_SERVICE.$NAMESPACE.svc.cluster.local/health > /dev/null; then
            echo "$(date): VM is healthy"
        else
            echo "$(date): VM health check failed!"
        fi
        
        sleep 30
    done
Create a monitoring pod
Create a file called health-monitor-pod.yaml:

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: health-monitor
  namespace: vm-health-probes
spec:
  containers:
  - name: monitor
    image: curlimages/curl:latest
    command: ["/bin/sh"]
    args: ["/scripts/check-health.sh"]
    volumeMounts:
    - name: script-volume
      mountPath: /scripts
  volumes:
  - name: script-volume
    configMap:
      name: health-check-script
      defaultMode: 0755
  restartPolicy: Always
Deploy the monitoring setup
# Apply the monitoring configuration
oc apply -f health-monitor-service.yaml
oc apply -f health-monitor-pod.yaml

# Check the monitoring pod logs
oc logs -f health-monitor
Subtask 3.4: Advanced Health Monitoring with Alerts
Let's set up more advanced monitoring with custom metrics.

Create a comprehensive health check
Create a file called advanced-health-check.yaml:

apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: CronJob
metadata:
  name: vm-health-checker
  namespace: vm-health-probes
spec:
  schedule: "*/2 * * * *"  # Every 2 minutes
  jobTemplate:
    spec:
      template:
        spec:
          containers:
          - name: health-checker
            image: curlimages/curl:latest
            command:
            - /bin/sh
            - -c
            - |
              echo "=== VM Health Check Report $(date) ==="
              
              # Check HTTP endpoint
              if curl -s -f http://vm-health-monitor.vm-health-probes.svc.cluster.local/health; then
                echo "✓ HTTP Health Check: PASSED"
              else
                echo "✗ HTTP Health Check: FAILED"
              fi
              
              # Check main page
              if curl -s -f http://vm-health-monitor.vm-health-probes.svc.cluster.local/; then
                echo "✓ Main Page Check: PASSED"
              else
                echo "✗ Main Page Check: FAILED"
              fi
              
              echo "=== End Health Check ==="
          restartPolicy: OnFailure
Deploy the advanced health checker
